<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7845676a90d406ac2ec661b4838c846021ee278c88b8de9a71f3e156757d8b08</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Axis of Iranian centrality' remains "one of more destabilising forces in the region", expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5746158ae67577dcd6adba05ef06096d721bdb8eb9c9950cd8ee90d1b43a7fff</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:46:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis launched a fresh barrage of missile and drone attacks on Saudi military targets on Monday, as Iran denied any involvement in the country's revived civil war. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr H. A. Hellyer, Senior Fellow in Geopolitics, International Security, and Middle East Studies at the Royal United Services Institute, says that Iran and its non-state proxies "remain to be one of the more destabilising forces in the region alongside the Israeli project of regional paramountcy".</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to boost Arctic role to tackle Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d669862f08c137560e6c5d7fa4c1f7dbf7e860631260773967e10639bb8f966</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Where is the kill switch? AI doomsday warnings trigger calls to regulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd427df7b6d1e9093d4c5f0d54587ccbf318cf245ea1c8ce569b96beacc88249</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:22:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260914-where-is-the-kill-switch-ai-doomsday-warnings-trigger-calls-to-regulate" /><summary type="html">Talk about doomsday scrolling. In the past week, our timelines have been alight with dark predictions of our imminent demise, including the one by a Silicon Valley engineer who puts a number on the chances of artificial intelligence wiping out humanity. Better than 10-percent. Triggering the wave of panic, the recent breach of the machine-learning programmers' site Hugging Face by AI machines who banded together to keep their nefarious deeds secret from their human overlords. Can machines actually destroy the planet on their own? In the age of technology, does problem solving always override safety?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to expand Arctic presence amid Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7427fabc12478ce4966a4a289a43da6140c4fdc0c3f468c694d6ff53f4a00ae2</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries on Monday called for the European Union to step up its presence in the Arctic, as melting ice opens new maritime routes while growing tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French candidates race to claim the cost-of-living issue ahead of 2027 vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11f9edc642ed43a299bae589988fa0714959db204a969ab94d367c0d06ed279e</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T16:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260914-french-candidates-race-to-claim-the-cost-of-living-issue-ahead-of-2027-vote" /><summary type="html">A new Ipsos survey reveals a country gripped by pessimism, with soaring prices the top worry for French voters ahead of the April 2027 presidential election. Candidates from far-right leader Marine Le Pen, to the far-left's Jean-Luc Mélenchon are racing to make the cost of living the defining issue of their campaigns.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Police arrested at least 63 people in anti-LGBT+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a767dc29394b636341351a108a2cbf3fc7d12bdce3df08c5b211af5af073864f</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:43:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-turkey-police-arrested-at-least-63-people-in-anti-lgbt-crackdown" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities on Sunday launched raids on gay bars, nightclubs, LGBTQ association offices and activists' homes in a sweeping crackdown in several cities as part of the government's "My Family is Safe" operations, Turkey's justice minister said.
 
More than 60 people were arrested, according to the state news agency, in raids condemned by human rights groups.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poll puts France's Le Pen in lead as presidential campaign kicks off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:198b450351af3ca46a24854412410d0d03077f15de0c2b1cb5dd6891a5d0e0ae</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:59:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-polls-put-france-s-le-pen-in-lead-as-presidential-campaign-kicks-off" /><summary type="html">France's far-right veteran candidate Marine Le Pen looks set to lead in the first round of elections next year, as the country's increasingly disillusioned voters seek real change, a poll of more than 13,000 voters has suggested.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian strike on train "terror knocking on EU's door'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f1442590b58485dd6e1b003de953735b4cdcffc4a5a68cb2b6690a49ddfa43d</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:57:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russian-strike-on-train-terror-knocking-on-eu-s-door" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin said on Monday it would keep striking targets across the "whole" of Ukraine, when asked about a rare drone attack on the Polish border that has rattled Warsaw and its European allies. NATO-member Poland said on Sunday that Russia had hit a railway locomotive inside Ukraine, about two kilometres (one mile) from their shared border, just days after Kyiv said it had hit a crossing at its border with Moldova.</summary></entry><entry><title>Investors weigh the potential cost of AI 'slowdown'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c9fdfa3ad677f5ca8ca8bbd02c1b8020046b370c8572c0a7bd67736fed75968</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:17:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260914-investors-weigh-the-potential-cost-of-ai-slowdown" /><summary type="html">The AI boom that has powered markets and unleashed a flood of investment is showing signs of strain. Calls to slow the development of powerful models fuel doubts over whether the sector's promised profits can justify its staggering costs.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Countries turn to coal to avoid shipping disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65a2e5fb12c894ecb110c083bf724f49bffe67e70364773895c673d351291a7f</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20260914-countries-turn-to-coal-to-avoid-shipping-disruptions-in-the-strait-of-hormuz--68a150198937.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20260914-countries-turn-to-coal-to-avoid-shipping-disruptions-in-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">The US-Israel war on Iran has shaken global energy markets and coal is no exception. Countries around the world are turning to the highly polluting source of power in a bid to avoid shipping disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz. According to the International Energy Agency, global coal demand is forecast to rise by ​1.2% this year to a record 8.94 billion ‌tonnes. FRANCE 24’s Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe has the details in this edition.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Keziah Jones goes symphonic</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2c16431c13fbf50cc858b1c4055f8d79af8b510428d6ce95e23f26f658dc1b8</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:55:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260914-keziah-jones-goes-symphonic--0f4900128715.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260914-keziah-jones-goes-symphonic" /><summary type="html">This week arts24 talks to Nigerian Blues Funk Artist Keziah Jones ahead of his Symphonic premier at la Scène Musicale on September 29 as part of Jazz &amp; Musique du Monde season. He tells FRANCE 24's Marjorie Hache about his music and about working with arranger Pierre Bertrand. Plus, we take a look at new releases by Beck, Miley Cyrus and Beabadobee.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>How will EU respond to Russian attack on train near Polish border?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dae823602003e7dd68b656b05843db11116bccc1b24ffaef0e66892cc9e1ad8</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:42:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-how-will-eu-respond-to-russian-attack-on-train-near-polish-border--acf1d7e6d739.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-how-will-eu-respond-to-russian-attack-on-train-near-polish-border" /><summary type="html">The EU's top diplomat said Monday that Russian strikes which hit a Warsaw-bound train near Ukraine's border with Poland shortly after top Western figures passed through were meant to "scare" off Kyiv's backers. "It is clearly meant to scare Western countries from supporting Ukraine, from going to Ukraine to show support," foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said, urging Kyiv's backers to do "the opposite". France 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>'What makes China work despite the pain in society?' asks analyst Dan Wang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0561276898a2b58e7b03f9f68a05d8cce71fad1e0a75de1f3a53410dbf85d9c</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang--d40c2ced80a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval speaks to Dan Wang, a China expert whose book ‘Breakneck:  China’s Quest to Engineer the Future’ is a New York Times bestseller. It takes a close look at Chinese life and draws from Wang’s own ten years of living there. Wang says the China and the US are some of the most similar people in the world, as they are both hustlers and take shortcuts.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>French 2027 presidential elections: Why Gen Z has mobilised for Mélenchon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37f43a85161b94f711f7e97a8602736a58f8bc8d578d470b425979987c6be1a7</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:05:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-french-2027-presidential-elections-why-gen-z-has-mobilised-for-m_lenchon--b3d1ffef001b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-french-2027-presidential-elections-why-gen-z-has-mobilised-for-m%C3%A9lenchon" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 French far-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc #Mélenchon is both highly controversial and a #GenZ favourite.
 
Mélenchon's young supporters express admiration for his promises to stage a "citizen's revolution",  redistrubute wealth, fight #climatechange and support #Palestine. The candidate's critics have accused him of complancency towards #Russia and antisemitism. 
 
Despite being divisive, recent polls predict that Mélenchon will qualify for the second round of #France's 2027 presidential #election, where he would likely face far-right candidate Marine #LePen.
 
So, why has France's Gen Z mobilised for Mélenchon?
 
🔴 FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler spoke to young voters to find out.</summary></entry><entry><title>Should the brakes be put on AI?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94b7acb6ad482347e8b9801c1547f9f277b45a7ed049b06a48ac59ffa4c87fce</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:02:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-should-the-brakes-be-put-on-ai--df0737934395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-should-the-brakes-be-put-on-ai" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says he is worried about America giving China an edge in the Artificial Intelligence market if too many rules and regulations are put on it. In recent days industry insiders, including top executives at Open AI and Anthropic, have once again sounded the alarm, saying that the way AI is being developed could threaten humanity and calling for more checks to be put in place.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump criticises 'negative forces' seeking to slow AI development</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d82d9346e51b34f803ba75b3a636b933af5770e7913b632ec00e403111ee0c</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:49:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development--bd4a498a26cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>Climate catastrophe leaves Nepal mourning while the search for the missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28c1f052e1fce79e6e129529164d688cab47a2e6411d2f21331f6f1af9eaa49d</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues--40d634ca2dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The himalayan flash flood that devastated northern Nepal on August 26 was an unprecedented disaster. The death toll continues to rise, with nearly 1,400 people now confirmed dead and 5,130 still missing, including around 600 foreign nationals from 35 countries.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Was Russian train strike meant to 'scare' the West?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92669076813aefdcf84b8a30776121ad294a606b8d8264f215d0ddd3506bcae8</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:41:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-was-russian-train-strike-meant-to-scare-the-west--eb42a4961f45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-was-russian-train-strike-meant-to-scare-the-west" /><summary type="html">The EU's top diplomat said Monday that Russian strikes which hit a Warsaw-bound train near Ukraine's border with Poland shortly after top Western figures passed through were meant to "scare" off Kyiv's backers. France 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg, has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Ukraine with drones as Poland warns of 'escalation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd1ef454cfecb8775979c6bd1d458f17281be8ffc157c297cff6d704d9d41b62</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:37:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russia-strikes-ukraine-with-drones-as-poland-warns-of-escalation--d24f4d1e5f89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russia-strikes-ukraine-with-drones-as-poland-warns-of-escalation" /><summary type="html">Russia continues its ramped-up air campaign against Ukraine, launching 453 drones in an overnight blitz. One drone struck 800 metres from a border crossing with Poland prompting the polish military to scramble fighter jets and helicopters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands rally in support of Brazil's Lula as election campaigning heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6883d5d5c35081ef9153b1af4d9b996c9368a6f6a4a56e5567617101d08354f9</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:59:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-thousands-rally-in-support-of-brazil-s-lula-as-election-campaigning-heats-up--a8fa79947199.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-thousands-rally-in-support-of-brazil-s-lula-as-election-campaigning-heats-up" /><summary type="html">With Brazil set to hold a Presidential election on October 4th, supporters of both incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula Da Silva and his main opponent Flavio Bolsonaro have been taking to the streets. Polls have the candidates, who are on opposite ends of political spectrum, neck and neck.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dozens arrested as Turkish police raid LGBTQ bars, activists' homes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f96370d9079a8ccb5d4efc570cdb43af71abbcad129f4450117a789c06b95cee</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:58:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-dozens-arrested-as-turkish-police-raid-lgbtq-bars-activists-homes--19f8c8b9504f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-dozens-arrested-as-turkish-police-raid-lgbtq-bars-activists-homes" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday made dozens of arrests in a slew of raids on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists. Authorities said the raids came in the context of the "Decade of the Family" proclaimed by Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan, aimed at "protecting our children, the institution of the family and social order".</summary></entry><entry><title>A 'complicated autumn' awaits Sweden after knife-edge vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe30dc3a2ded0e2f0d71c526182565e2996a4b905482c9b8d505ca3abe3a04e0</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:56:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-a-complicated-autumn-awaits-sweden-after-knife-edge-vote--b980c5153729.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-a-complicated-autumn-awaits-sweden-after-knife-edge-vote" /><summary type="html">Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90 percent of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘They drove us from our land’: Thousands displaced by Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd05c423b0a3456e2e7f26cce057d776c7a654750a98757348f81ff90935aea</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:22:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-they-drove-us-from-our-land-thousands-displaced-by-yemen-conflict--560bed71a167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-they-drove-us-from-our-land-thousands-displaced-by-yemen-conflict" /><summary type="html">According to the UN, more than 86,000 people have been displaced in Yemen since July, following fighting between the Iran-backed Houthis rebels and government forces. Many have fled to refugee camps in government-controlled Aden, while others have headed to neighbouring Djibouti.</summary></entry></feed>
